Example 18. Evaluate the complete elliptic integral
\Pi(\delta\backslash30^{0}) to 5D.
From 17.7.14 we have
\Pi(\delta\backslash30^{0})=K(30^{0})+\tfrac{\pi}{2}\sqrt{\frac{40}{9}}\;[1-\Lambda_{0}(\epsilon\backslash30^{0})]\]

where \(\epsilon=\arcsin[(1-n)/\cos^2\alpha]^{1/2}=45^{\circ}\). Thus using Table 17.8
\Pi(\delta\backslash30^{0})=2.80099.
Table 17.9 gives 2.80126 by 6 point Lagrangian interpolation. The discrepancy results from interpolation with respect to n for \(\varphi=90^{\circ}\) in Table 17.9.
